.Dd June 9, 2026
.Dt EFIBOOTMGR 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm efibootmgr
.Nd inspect and modify the UEFI Boot Manager
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl v
.Nm
.Fl c
.Fl d Ar disk
.Fl l Ar loader
.Op Fl p Ar partnum
.Op Fl L Ar label
.Nm
.Fl B
.Fl b Ar NNNN
.Nm
.Fl o Ar bootorder | Fl O
.Nm
.Fl n Ar NNNN | Fl N
.Nm
.Fl t Ar seconds | Fl T
.Nm
.Brq Fl a | Fl A
.Fl b Ar NNNN
.Nm
.Fl f | Fl F
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility displays and updates the boot configuration held by the UEFI
firmware in non-volatile RAM.
The configuration is a set of UEFI variables in the global namespace,
.Pq Sy 8be4df61-93ca-11d2-aa0d-00e098032b8c ,
the most important of which are:
.Bl -tag -width BootCurrent
.It Sy BootOrder
The sequence in which the firmware tries the boot entries below.
.It Sy Boot Ns Ar NNNN
An individual boot entry, where
.Ar NNNN
is a four-hex-digit identifier.
Each one names a description and a UEFI device path that points to a
loader.
.It Sy BootCurrent
The entry the firmware actually used on the current boot.
Read-only from the operating system's perspective.
.It Sy BootNext
An override that, when present, makes the firmware boot the named entry
once and then revert to
.Sy BootOrder .
.It Sy Timeout
How many seconds the firmware shows its menu before booting
.Sy BootOrder Ns Bq 0 .
.El
.Pp
Without a mutating option, or when
.Fl v
is given,
.Nm
prints the current state of these variables, one per line, with each
.Sy Boot Ns Ar NNNN
rendered on its own line.
A mutating invocation is otherwise silent on success;
.Fl c
reports the number of the entry it created.
.Pp
All operations require the kernel
.Xr efi 4D
driver and the
.Sy PRIV_SYS_CONFIG
privilege.
.Sh OPTIONS
The following options are supported:
.Bl -tag -width Fl
.It Fl a | Fl A
Set
.Pq Fl a
or clear
.Pq Fl A
the
.Sy LOAD_OPTION_ACTIVE
bit on the entry selected with
.Fl b .
Inactive entries are skipped by the boot manager.
.It Fl b Ar NNNN
Boot entry to operate on, in hexadecimal.
Used together with
.Fl a , Fl A ,
or
.Fl B .
.It Fl B
Delete the
.Sy Boot Ns Ar NNNN
entry selected with
.Fl b
and remove its number from
.Sy BootOrder .
.It Fl c
Create a new
.Sy Boot Ns Ar NNNN
entry.
The lowest unused number is allocated, the entry is set active, and its
number is prepended to
.Sy BootOrder .
Requires
.Fl d
and
.Fl l ;
the EFI System Partition is located automatically
.Pq see Fl p .
.It Fl d Ar disk
Disk whose GPT is read to locate the partition.
Either a full
.Pa /dev/rdsk
path, or a disk name such as
.Ar c0t0d0 ,
which is resolved to its whole-disk raw device.
.It Fl f | Fl F
Set
.Pq Fl f
or clear
.Pq Fl F
the
.Sy BOOT_TO_FW_UI
bit in
.Sy OsIndications .
After
.Fl f ,
the next reboot drops into the firmware setup UI instead of running the
boot manager, so that
.Ql efibootmgr -f
followed by a reboot is the equivalent of the Linux command
.Ql systemctl reboot \-\-firmware-setup .
The firmware must advertise support via
.Sy OsIndicationsSupported ;
if it does not,
.Fl f
fails.
.It Fl l Ar loader
UEFI loader path inside the ESP, relative to its root.
Both
.Sq /
and
.Sq \e
are accepted as separators, so for example
.Ar /EFI/illumos/loader64.efi
names the loader.
A path written with backslashes must be quoted to survive the shell.
.It Fl L Ar label
Human-readable label for the new entry.
The default is
.Sy illumos .
.It Fl n Ar NNNN
Set
.Sy BootNext
to the given entry.
The firmware boots it once and then returns to
.Sy BootOrder .
.It Fl N
Delete
.Sy BootNext .
.It Fl o Ar bootorder
Set
.Sy BootOrder .
.Ar bootorder
is a comma-separated list of boot entry numbers in hexadecimal, for
example
.Ar 0001,0000,0002 .
.It Fl O
Delete
.Sy BootOrder .
.It Fl p Ar partnum
Slice number of the EFI System Partition on
.Ar disk ,
numbered from 0 as elsewhere in illumos.
This option is normally unnecessary:
.Nm
uses the disk's EFI System Partition, which is the partition the firmware
boots.
Give
.Fl p
only to choose between several EFI System Partitions on one disk.
.It Fl t Ar seconds
Set
.Sy Timeout .
.It Fl T
Delete
.Sy Timeout .
.It Fl v
When listing, also print the EFI device path of every entry.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Pa
.It Pa /dev/efi
UEFI Runtime Services driver.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It 0
Successful completion.
.It 1
A runtime error occurred, such as a firmware or driver failure.
.It 2
Invalid command-line options were specified.
.El
.Sh INTERFACE STABILITY
The command line interface of
.Nm
is
.Sy Committed .
The output of
.Nm
is
.Sy Not-an-Interface
and may change at any time.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr efi 4D ,
.Xr bootadm 8 ,
.Xr installboot 8
